    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0529" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg501"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">330/9–353: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Deputy United States Representative at the united
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wadsworth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-09-03T13:50:00-04:00">September 3,
                            1953—1:50 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>151. Regarding Turk SC candidacy, reference Department telegram 87, yesterday
                    during translation in Security Council meeting, I spoke with Crosthwaite (United
                    Kingdom) closely following arguments set forth reference telegram. He felt
                    essence their original question still unanswered, unless key words were “firm
                    support”. He suggested this meant we would do more than simply vote for Turkey.
                    I agreed, with limitation that United States would not wave flags and beat drums
                    for Turkey, nor do all work necessary to assure her success.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wadsworth</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
